    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/716F3DBB868513EDA5A7657F756BBDD8/jobs/345841": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Counselor",
      "description": "Financial Aid Counselor You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Financial Aid Counselor Columbia College - Columbia, SC 29203 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Education Level 4 Year Degree Category Education Apply Description JOB SUMMARY The role of Financial Aid Counselor is to support students and families in navigating financial aid processes. The  Financial Aid Counselor will continuously evaluate students’ eligibility, perform initial and adjustments to student financial aid packaging throughout the year and reconcile financial aid provided to students. This Counselor is expected to providing expert advice to ensure students have access to the resources they need while maintaining data integrity and ensure compliance with institutional, state, and federal regulations. Qualifications ESSENTIAL JOB FUNCTIONS: Student Advising: Provide comprehensive counseling to students and families about financial aid options, application procedures, and eligibility requirements. Eligibility Assessment: Verify and assess student applications for compliance with program regulations and institutional policies. Program Coordination: Manage federal, state, and institutional financial aid programs, ensuring effective implementation and compliance. Compliance & Documentation: Maintain up-to-date knowledge of federal and state regulations, ensuring strict adherence in all processes. Keep detailed records and documentation for assigned student cases. Process Improvement: Utilize professional judgment to resolve unique student situations and contribute to the optimization of financial aid processes. Data Management: Ensure data integrity within financial aid systems, utilizing tools such as Jenzabar, PowerFAIDS, and Department of Education software. Outreach & Training: Participate in on-campus and off-campus workshops and training sessions to enhance financial aid awareness and expertise. Collaboration: Work independently and as part of a team to meet office objectives and maintain excellent customer service standards. Seamless student financial services: Work with all student service areas but especially Tuition Accounts to coordinate of aid and billing throughout all stages of awarding, disbursing, refunding &financial clearance. Communications Support: Working with financial aid leadership, assist with developing financial aid communications and financial literacy improvements to support our students completion of financial aid requirements. This includes targeted outreach to various student populations and aid statuses. Other Duties: Perform additional responsibilities as assigned to support the Office of Financial Aid. MINIMUM REQUIREMENTS TO PERFORM WORK: Bachelor’s degree or relevant experience in financial aid administration Familiarity with federal, state, and institutional financial aid programs. Strong organizational, interpersonal, and communication skills. Ability to handle confidential information with professionalism and discretion. Flexibility to work evenings and weekends as needed. Experience coordinating satisfactory academic progress programs. Exceptional customer service and adaptability in a dynamic environment. Analytical and problem-solving abilities. Preferred: 1-2 years of relevant experience in financial aid, higher education, or a related field. Experience with Jenzabar and PowerFAIDS systems. Knowledge of Department of Education software, including EDconnect, COD, FAA Access to CPS Online, and NSLDS. Experience coordinating satisfactory academic progress programs. PHYSICAL DEMANDS: Requires sedentary work that involves walking, standing, lifting, carrying, pushing and pulling some of the time and requires the ability to lift up to 50 pounds and the ability to exert up to 10 pounds of force on a recurring basis or routine keyboard operations. WORKING CONDITIONS: Work environment risks exposure to no known environmental hazards. APPLICATION PROCESS: Application review process will start immediately until the position is filled. Interested candidates should complete an online application and upload a cover letter and resume with your online application. EOE M/F/D/V Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/716F3DBB868513EDA5A7657F756BBDD8/jobs/345834": {
      "title": "Open-Rank Faculty in Social Work & COR",
      "description": "Open-Rank Faculty in Social Work & COR You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Open-Rank Faculty in Social Work & COR Columbia College - Columbia, SC 29203 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply Description | POSITION SUMMARY Columbia College invites applications for an open-rank position in Social Work and with the Center for Organization Resilience (COR) that will begin in August 2027 . The position is housed in the School of Arts and Sciences and reports to the Dean of Arts and Sciences . The COR program at Columbia College builds Trauma Informed Empowered Resilient (TIER) organizations through intentional workshops based on the six principles of trauma informed approaches (SAMHSA, 2023).  The position requires an experienced lecturer who will deliver dynamic social work lectures and engaging relevant content with students, the community, and organizations. Columbia College seeks candidates who aspire to excellence in teaching, leadership, and research, and who can build collaborative relationships within the college and the profession. Typical Job Duties for the Lecturer / COR Facilitator: Instruct and facilitate a learning experience in person and/or online for BSW students using CSWE accredited and approved curriculum Responsible for the duties of a full-time faculty member as outlined in the Columbia College Handbook Some recruitment, retention, and marketing activities for the BSW and COR programs Learn and Facilitate the Trauma Informed Empowered Resilience (TIER) Leadership curriculum with COR organizations pursuing certification in trauma informed approaches BSW faculty teach courses in the intersection of social work and child welfare or criminal justice, direct service with individuals and groups and macro practice. This position is a nine-month appointment. Faculty Rank is dependent upon qualifications. The standard teaching load is twelve credit hours (4/4) for the fall and spring semesters. The successful candidate must demonstrate the ability to design and deliver courses in a variety of formats, including online and hybrid modalities, and is expected to teach core courses in Social Work. Faculty are expected to have flexibility in class scheduling to meet the needs of the students. Faculty members are also expected to participate in faculty governance and academic program activities and to engage in service as well as scholarship and professional development. | ABOUT COLUMBIA COLLEGE Founded in 1854, Columbia College is a private liberal arts institution offering undergraduate, graduate, and online programs. The College combines a liberal arts foundation with career-focused preparation and emphasizes small classes, faculty mentorship, inquiry-based learning, and community engagement. The College provides educational opportunities that develop students’ capacity for critical thought and expression, lifelong learning and acceptance of personal responsibility. Columbia College empowers students to change the world with Courage for Innovation, Commitment to Social Justice, Confidence through Service, and Competence in Leadership. In furtherance of its mission, the College is responsive to the needs of students, the communities to which it belongs, and the greater global society. Qualifications | QUALIFICATIONS Each successful candidate must have an earned Master of Social Work by the time of appointment. A terminal degree in Social Work is not required but preferred ( DSW or PhD ). The successful candidate must have a minimum of three years of full-time teaching experience and five years as a licensed social worker practicing in the field.  All required documents must be completed for the application to be reviewed. | APPLICATION PROCESS To apply, candidates must submit the following materials through the online submission portal (all in one pdf file except for the cover letter, which may be uploaded as a separate document): A cover letter describing teaching i nterests and experiences A current curriculum vitae A formal statement that addresses teaching philosophy and methodology A formal statement regarding research and other scholarly endeavors Names and contact information for three references Copies of graduate transcripts (unofficial copies of transcripts will suffice for the initial stage) Review of completed applications will begin in October and continue until the position is filled. All required documents must be completed for the application to be reviewed. Copies of official transcripts will be required of the selected finalist. If interested in applying for this position, submit the above materials through the online submission website at https:// www.columbiasc.edu/about/employment. If you have any additional questions regarding the position, please contact Dr. David McCracken, Dean of Arts & Sciences via email at dmccracken@columbiasc.edu . | EQUAL OPPORTUNITY AND ACCOMMODATIONS Columbia College is an affirmative action and equal opportunity employer. Columbia College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, ancestry, national origin, gender, identity sexual orientation, marital status, religion, age, disability, national origin, results of genetic testing, or service in the military. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/716F3DBB868513EDA5A7657F756BBDD8/jobs/345825": {
      "title": "Open-Rank Faculty in Biology",
      "description": "Open-Rank Faculty in Biology You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Open-Rank Faculty in Biology Columbia College - Columbia, SC 29203 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply Description | POSITION SUMMARY The School of Health Sciences at Columbia College invites applications for an open-rank faculty position in Biology , with appointment up to the rank of Associate Professor, beginning August 2027 .  The College seeks a broadly trained biologist whose primary expertise is in genetics.  Additional expertise in epidemiology, anatomy and physiology, molecular biology, cellular biology, microbiology, bioinformatics, or another related biological subdiscipline is highly desirable. Candidates considered for the rank of assistant and associate must demonstrate the potential to pursue a balanced commitment to excellent teaching, active professional and community service, and productive research.  The successful candidate will primarily teach undergraduate courses in genetics , as well as introductory biology and other courses that support the biology program and the broader needs of the School of Health Sciences.  Depending on the candidate’s expertise, additional teaching assignments may include epidemiology, anatomy and physiology, cell and molecular biology, microbiology, or other upper-level biology courses. This position offers an excellent opportunity to contribute to the continued development of Biology and the growth of the School of Health Sciences, which includes programs in Biology, Chemistry, Environmental Health, Exercise Science, Public Health, and Speech-Language Pathology .  The successful candidate will join a collaborative group of faculty committed to student-centered teaching, experiential learning, undergraduate research, and preparation for careers and graduate study in the biological, chemical, biomedical and health sciences. This is a full-time , nine-month , tenure-track or non-tenure-track position, depending on the candidate’s qualifications and assigned rank.  The standard teaching load is twelve credit hours during each of the fall and spring semesters.  Faculty members are expected to have flexibility in class scheduling to meet program and College needs.  Summer teaching may be available based on enrollment needs. | ABOUT COLUMBIA COLLEGE Founded in 1854, Columbia College is a private liberal arts institution committed to preparing students for lives of purpose, responsibility, and impact. Since its founding, the College has cultivated a learning environment where academic rigor is paired with a deep investment in personal growth, ethical leadership, and community engagement. Students are encouraged to engage deeply with their communities, take initiative, and approach challenges with resilience. Whether in the classroom, through service, or in professional settings, they learn to lead with empathy and integrity. The College offers undergraduate, graduate, and online programs that blend a liberal arts foundation with career-focused preparation. Small class sizes and close faculty mentorship foster a culture of support. Qualifications | KEY RESPONSIBILITIES The ideal candidate will: Teach genetics, introductory biology, and other undergraduate biology courses consistent with the candidate’s expertise and program needs. Develop and deliver engaging, outcomes-based instruction for a culturally and economically diverse student population using appropriate laboratory and experiential learning approaches. Develop laboratory, computational, or community-based learning experiences that help students connect biological concepts with biomedical, environmental, and public health applications. Maintain an active scholarly agenda appropriate to the candidate’s rank and appointment. Mentor students in independent research, internships, professional development, and preparation for employment or graduate programs. Provide service to the Biology program, School of Health Sciences, College, profession, and broader community. Participate in faculty governance, professional development, and other duties consistent with the expectations of a full-time faculty appointment. | MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Tenure-Track Appointment Earned doctorate in Biology or closely related discipline from a regionally accredited institution. Evidence of, or demonstrated potential for, effective undergraduate teaching. Evidence of, or demonstrated potential for, a productive scholarly agenda appropriate for promotion and tenure. Non-Tenure Track Appointment Master’s degree in Biology or closely related discipline from a regionally accredited institution. Demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, service, and professional experience. | PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Preference will be given to candidates who demonstrate one or more of the following: Expertise in genetics, genomics, or molecular genetics. Experience using and teaching bioinformatics, computational biology, biostatistics, or biological data analysis. Ability to teach epidemiology, anatomy and physiology, molecular or cellular biology, microbiology, or another area that complements the Biology curriculum. A scholarly agenda that is feasible within a primarily undergraduate institution and provides opportunities for student participation. | APPLICATION PROCESS Candidates must apply online through the Columbia College website application portal ( www.columbiasc.edu/about/employment ).  Applicants should be prepared to attach the following: A letter of application/interest A current curriculum vitae List of at least three references with current email addresses and phone numbers Statement of teaching philosophy Copies of graduate transcripts (unofficial copies of transcripts will suffice for the initial stage) References will be contacted and asked to submit letters of recommendation to the Committee Chair. Depending on the rank, evidence of scholarly activity may be requested.  Please submit all documents in one combined pdf file .  Review of applications will begin October 1, 2026 , and continue until the position is filled. | EQUAL OPPORTUNITY AND ACCOMMODATIONS Columbia College is an affirmative action and equal opportunity employer. Columbia College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, ancestry, national origin, gender, identity sexual orientation, marital status, religion, age, disability, national origin, results of genetic testing, or service in the military. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/716F3DBB868513EDA5A7657F756BBDD8/jobs/345808": {
      "title": "Dean of School of Education",
      "description": "Dean of School of Education You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Dean of School of Education Columbia College - Columbia, SC 29203 Apply Overview Position Type Full Time Apply Description | THE OPPORTUNITY Columbia College seeks an innovative educator and strategic leader for the position of Dean of the School of Education to begin July 1, 2027 . The School of Education is a cornerstone of Columbia College’s mission, housing seven undergraduate and four graduate academic programs. Backed by more than $12 million in state and federal grants, the incoming Dean will inherit a highly successful team. Columbia College seeks an accomplished leader who will guide the School of Education into its next chapter of growth, with a strategic focus on innovation, expanded community partnerships, and the development of new advanced graduate curricula, including doctoral-level programming. | THE ROLE OF THE POSITION The Dean of the School of Education reports to the Provost/Executive Vice President for Academic Affairs and serves as a member of the Senior Leadership Team. The School of Education is home to two distinct Centers of Excellence awarded by the South Carolina Commission on Higher Education: one in Alternative Certification and one in Mathematics. The School also proudly hosts the Call Me MISTER and South Carolina Teaching Fellows programs. Known for its dedication to the community, the School of Education maintains a robust focus on multilingual learners and special education through deep-rooted institutional partnerships. | ABOUT COLUMBIA COLLEGE Columbia College is a private liberal arts institution committed to preparing students for lives of purpose, responsibility, and impact. Since its founding, the College has cultivated a learning environment where academic rigor is paired with a deep investment in personal growth, ethical leadership, and community engagement. Students are encouraged to engage deeply with their communities, take initiative, and approach challenges with resilience. Whether in the classroom, through service, or in professional settings, they learn to lead with empathy and integrity. The College offers undergraduate, graduate, and online programs that blend a liberal arts foundation with career-focused preparation. Small class sizes and close faculty mentorship foster a culture of support. | THE HISTORY Founded in 1854 and rooted in the United Methodist Church, Columbia College is one of the oldest institutions of higher learning in South Carolina. Established as Columbia Female College, it opened in 1859 with a mission to provide women a rigorous liberal arts education. The College became fully coeducational in 2020 and welcomed its first coeducational residential class in 2021. The College has demonstrated resilience and adaptability throughout its history. The campus rebuilt after fires, including the 1964 fire that destroyed Old Main. Its surviving columns remain a College symbol and are incorporated into the institutional logo. Today, Columbia College offers an inclusive, personalized education centered on critical thinking, effective communication, lifelong learning, and personal responsibility. Qualifications | KEY RESPONSIBILITIES The Dean will provide overall leadership to the School of Education in the following ways: Oversight of curriculum and programs: develop new programs, coordinate program review and accreditation process with program chairs, supervise the assessment of the programs within the school, promote programs within the school; Oversight of accreditation and state department requirements of the Education Program Provider (EPP): coordinate state report submissions with Director of Teacher Education (DTE) and Field Experience Coordinator, organize and lead accreditation cycle requirements with DTE and program chairs; Hire, develop, and supervise faculty and academic support staff: oversee hiring process of faculty, orient and support development of new faculty with assistance of program chairs, coordinate peer-review of teaching, oversee student course evaluations, evaluate faculty annually (teaching, service, and scholarship, as appropriate for faculty position), recommend faculty for tenure and promotion, oversee advising, hire and orient adjunct faculty with assistance of program chairs, conduct/coordinate in-class observations of new adjunct faculty, review faculty loads and assignments with each faculty member at the beginning of each academic year; Maintain a positive working environment; Tend to academic student issues; Manage resources, including proposing and monitoring budgets; Serve as a liaison with administration and other College departments; Work with admissions to recruit new students; Work with marketing to develop consistent, on-brand collateral materials; Represent the College externally when appropriate; Maintain and share program and school data as appropriate; Complete other duties as assigned. | QUALIFICATIONS Holds or has held a valid educator certification; Has an earned doctorate (Ph.D. or Ed.D.) in Education from an accredited institution; Has at least 5 years of successful public school teaching experience; Is knowledgeable/has experience with the certification requirements in the state of South Carolina or other US state; Has experience with accreditation through a national or state process and specialty program areas (SPA) reports; Has a minimum of 3 years of progressive academic leadership experience, such as department chair or associate dean; Has a distinguished record of teaching, scholarship, and service for more than 5 years, qualifying for a senior faculty rank; Experience with submission and monitoring of state and federal grants is desired; Experience with doctoral program development at the advanced level is desired. | APPLICATIONS INQUIRIES AND NOMINATIONS Candidates must apply online through the Columbia College website application portal ( www.columbiasc.edu/about/employment ).  Applicants should be prepared to attach the following: A letter of application/interest Current curriculum vitae List of at least three references with current email addresses and phone numbers (references will not be contacted until final stages and only after candidates have been informed) Statement of teaching philosophy Copies of graduate transcripts (transcripts may be unofficial but official would be submitted upon hire). Depending on the rank, evidence of scholarly activity may be requested. Please submit all documents in one combined pdf file . Review of applications will begin October 1, 2026, and continue until the position is filled . | COLUMBIA SOUTH CAROLINA Columbia is the capital of South Carolina with a growing metropolitan population of over 800,000. The city is a central hub for government, healthcare, and commerce, and is home to more than 40,000 college students, contributing to a vibrant academic and research community. The city’s central location in the state's geographic center provides convenient access to the Atlantic coast and the Blue Ridge Mountains. Columbia’s downtown features over 70 restaurants and shops, with ongoing investment in infrastructure, housing, and public spaces. The Main Street District , Five Points , the Vista , and The Bull Street District have become key destinations for dining, arts, and community events, including the weekly Soda City Market , where vendors must make or grow their own products. The city supports a range of cultural institutions, including the Columbia Museum of Art , the South Carolina State Museum , and the Nickelodeon Theatre , S outh Carolina’s only nonprofit art house cinema. Columbia is also home to the Columbia Fireflies , the city’s minor league baseball team. Outdoor amenities are easily accessible, including the Three Rivers Greenway , which connects parks and neighborhoods along the Congaree, Saluda, and Broad Rivers. Just outside the city, Congaree National Park offers hiking and kayaking opportunities in one of the country's largest old-growth bottomland hardwood forests . | EQUAL OPPORTUNITY AND ACCOMMODATIONS Columbia College is an affirmative action and equal opportunity employer. Columbia College does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, ancestry, national origin, gender, identity sexual orientation, marital status, religion, age, disability, national origin, results of genetic testing, or service in the military. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
